<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional Qualitative Results</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further demonstrate the consistent performance of our proposed goal representation, this section provides additional qualitative examples from our ablation study. The scenarios presented in Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix A Additional Qualitative Results ‣ Efficient Virtuoso: A Latent Diffusion Transformer Model for Goal-Conditioned Trajectory Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix A Additional Qualitative Results ‣ Efficient Virtuoso: A Latent Diffusion Transformer Model for Goal-Conditioned Trajectory Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, and <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix A Additional Qualitative Results ‣ Efficient Virtuoso: A Latent Diffusion Transformer Model for Goal-Conditioned Trajectory Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> reinforce the conclusions drawn in Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Results and Analysis ‣ Efficient Virtuoso: A Latent Diffusion Transformer Model for Goal-Conditioned Trajectory Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Across a variety of intersection geometries and turn types, we consistently observe the same behavioral patterns. The <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No Goal</span> model correctly identifies the multi-modal nature of the decision space but cannot commit to a single plan. The <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Endpoint Goal</span> model resolves the strategic ambiguity but suffers from tactical imprecision, often generating geometrically unnatural paths. Our proposed <span id="A1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sparse Route</span> model consistently produces a tight, uni-modal distribution of trajectories that are both strategically correct and tactically precise, closely matching the ground truth.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.03658v1/figures/ablation_row1.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/108;" width="476" height="108" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Qualitative results for a left turn at a complex, multi-lane intersection. The <span id="A1.F5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Endpoint Goal</span> model’s predictions (center) exhibit significant variance and imprecision compared to our proposed model (right).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.03658v1/figures/ablation_row2.png" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/141;" width="476" height="141" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Qualitative results for a standard, 90-degree left turn. The superiority of the path-aware <span id="A1.F6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Sparse Route</span> goal is evident in the precision of the generated trajectory arc.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.03658v1/figures/ablation_row3.png" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/150;" width="476" height="150" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Qualitative results for another left turn scenario. Our model (right) correctly infers the need for a smooth, curved path, while the <span id="A1.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Endpoint</span> model (center) generates trajectories that unnaturally cut the corner.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
